["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The right load kills cleanly. Non toxic shot for ducks is the law. One rifle load, zeroed, beats a drawer of mixed boxes.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Which gun and load for which hunt. Tikka .308: deer, 150 to 165 grain hunting bullet. 12 gauge: ducks and geese, steel number 2 or 3, non toxic only. 12 gauge: grouse and quail, number 6 to 7.5 shot. CZ 457 .22: grouse only, head shots.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your guns, your loads</text>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"38\" width=\"120\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"56\">Gun</text>\n    <rect x=\"132\" y=\"38\" width=\"110\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"142\" y=\"56\">Hunt</text>\n    <rect x=\"244\" y=\"38\" width=\"146\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"254\" y=\"56\">Load</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"68\" width=\"380\" height=\"54\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n    <text x=\"20\" y=\"92\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tikka .308</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"92\">Deer</text><text x=\"254\" y=\"92\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">150 to 165 gr</text><text x=\"254\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\">one load, zeroed</text>\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"126\" width=\"380\" height=\"54\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" fill-opacity=\".18\"/>\n    <text x=\"20\" y=\"150\" font-weight=\"bold\">12 gauge</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"150\">Ducks, geese</text><text x=\"254\" y=\"150\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Steel #2 or #3</text><text x=\"254\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\">non toxic only</text>\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"184\" width=\"380\" height=\"54\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n    <text x=\"20\" y=\"208\" font-weight=\"bold\">12 gauge</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"208\">Grouse, quail</text><text x=\"254\" y=\"208\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">#6 to #7.5</text><text x=\"254\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"14\">1 to 1 1/8 oz</text>\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"242\" width=\"380\" height=\"54\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" fill-opacity=\".15\"/>\n    <text x=\"20\" y=\"266\" font-weight=\"bold\">CZ 457 .22</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"266\">Grouse only</text><text x=\"254\" y=\"266\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">.22 LR</text><text x=\"254\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\">head shots (Tip)</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Ducks: <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Non toxic shot\">Non toxic shot</button> only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. No .22 for quail <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>.22 LR means .22 long rifle. Gr means grains, a bullet weight.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full key points</summary><ul><li><strong>.308 for deer:</strong> a 150 to 165 gr (grain) hunting bullet does the job <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><strong>One load rule:</strong> pick one .308 load, zero with it, hunt with it (Tip).</li><li><strong>Ducks:</strong> non toxic shot only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Steel #2 or #3 is the all round choice <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Quail and grouse:</strong> #6 to #7.5 shot, 1 to 1 1/8 oz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><strong>.22 LR (long rifle):</strong> legal for grouse <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Head shots only (Tip). Not legal for quail: use the shotgun <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Buy 3 to 4 boxes of the <strong>same lot</strong> of .308 if you can (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\".308 bullet weights, heavier to the right. 150 grain, cup and core, for deer. 165 to 168 grain, bonded or Partition, for deer, black bear and all round. 178 to 180 grain, bonded, Partition or all copper, for elk and moose later. Cutaways show a lead core in a copper jacket, and an all copper bullet.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">.308 bullets: heavier for bigger game</text>\n  <!-- bullet 1 -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(70 0)\">\n    <path d=\"M-16 200 L-16 120 Q -16 80 0 60 Q 16 80 16 120 L16 200 Z\" fill=\"#c87533\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <path d=\"M-11 196 L-11 122 Q -11 92 0 76 Q 11 92 11 122 L11 196 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f88\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(200 0)\">\n    <path d=\"M-16 200 L-16 110 Q -16 70 0 50 Q 16 70 16 110 L16 200 Z\" fill=\"#c87533\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <path d=\"M-11 196 L-11 112 Q -11 82 0 66 Q 11 82 11 112 L11 196 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f88\"/>\n    <path d=\"M-11 150 H11\" stroke=\"#c87533\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(330 0)\">\n    <path d=\"M-16 200 L-16 100 Q -16 60 0 40 Q 16 60 16 100 L16 200 Z\" fill=\"#c87533\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"70\" y=\"224\">150 gr</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"224\">165 to 168 gr</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"224\">178 to 180 gr</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"70\" y=\"246\">Deer</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\">Deer, black bear</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"246\">Elk, moose</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"70\" y=\"266\">Cup and core</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\">Bonded, Partition</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"266\">Bonded or copper</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"280\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#8a8f88\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"291\">lead core</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"280\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#c87533\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"291\">copper</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"291\">Not to scale</text></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Deer near Kamloops: <strong>150 gr cup and core</strong> is plenty (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the table and bullet types</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Animal</th><th>Bullet weight</th><th>Bullet type</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Deer</td><td>150 gr</td><td>Cup and core is fine</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Deer, black bear, all round</td><td>165 to 168 gr</td><td>Bonded or Partition for heavy bone</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Elk, moose (later)</td><td>178 to 180 gr</td><td>Bonded, Partition or monolithic copper</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Gr means grains, a bullet weight unit. 7,000 grains make 1 pound <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Cup and core: lead core in a copper jacket. Cheap and accurate, expands fast <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Bonded and Partition: hold together through bone <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Monolithic copper: all copper, deep penetration, lead free <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>One box each of 2 deer loads at the range. Keep the one that groups best. Buy 3 more boxes of it.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Same rifle, same zero, two loads. Load A, the one you zeroed with, groups on the bullseye. Load B groups somewhere else. Switch loads and you must re zero.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Same zero, different load</text>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"220\" height=\"220\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"150\" r=\"80\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"150\" r=\"44\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"150\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f6b3a\"><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"146\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"136\" cy=\"154\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"140\" r=\"6\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#4a7fb0\"><circle cx=\"186\" cy=\"96\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"196\" cy=\"106\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"182\" cy=\"110\" r=\"6\"/></g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\"><circle cx=\"262\" cy=\"80\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\"/><text x=\"278\" y=\"86\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Load A</text><text x=\"278\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">zeroed with it</text>\n    <circle cx=\"262\" cy=\"150\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"278\" y=\"156\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Load B</text><text x=\"278\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">hits elsewhere</text></g>\n  <rect x=\"254\" y=\"206\" width=\"136\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"322\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Switch load?</text><text x=\"322\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Re zero</text>\n  <text x=\"130\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Example only. Your gap will differ</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Switch loads and you must <strong>re zero</strong> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the details</summary><ul><li>Every load hits a different spot from the same zero <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Switch loads and you must re zero <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Write the load name and lot number on your zero card (Tip).</li><li>Never mix boxes in your pocket on a hunt (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Shot size by bird, pellets drawn at relative size. Steel number 4 for teal and very close shots. Steel 3 for medium ducks and decoying birds. Steel 2 for all round ducks. Steel BB for geese. Upland: number 7.5 for quail, number 6 for grouse. Bigger number means smaller pellet.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shot size by bird</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bigger number = smaller pellet</text>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"50\" width=\"380\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"67\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">Waterfowl: steel (non toxic)</text>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"96\" r=\"6.5\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"101\" font-weight=\"bold\">#4</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"101\">Teal, very close</text>\n    <circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"126\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"131\" font-weight=\"bold\">#3</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"131\">Medium ducks, decoying</text>\n    <circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"157\" r=\"7.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"162\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">#2</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"162\" font-weight=\"bold\">All round ducks</text>\n    <circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"190\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"195\" font-weight=\"bold\">BB</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"195\">Geese</text>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"214\" width=\"380\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"231\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">Upland: lead or steel</text>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"256\" r=\"4.8\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"261\" font-weight=\"bold\">#7.5</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"261\">Quail</text>\n    <circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"282\" r=\"5.5\" fill=\"#8a8f88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"287\" font-weight=\"bold\">#6</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"287\">Grouse</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"390\" y=\"287\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Relative size</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Non toxic only for ducks, geese, coots and snipe <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. <strong>Steel #2</strong> is the all round duck load <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: loads, speeds, exceptions</summary><ul><li>Non toxic shot is required for ducks, geese, coots and snipe: steel, bismuth, tungsten, tin <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Pigeons and doves are the exception <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Steel shot\">Steel shot</button> #2: all round duck load <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Steel #3: medium ducks and close decoying birds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Steel #4: teal and very close shots <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Steel BB: geese <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>About 1 1/8 to 1 1/4 oz at 1,400 to 1,550 fps (feet per second). More pellets beats more speed <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Steel</th><th>Bismuth</th><th>Tungsten, TSS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Feel</td><td>Hard</td><td>Softer, like lead</td><td>Very dense</td></tr><tr><td>Best for</td><td>New 3 inch gun</td><td>Older guns, fixed chokes</td><td>Long range</td></tr><tr><td>Cost</td><td>Lowest</td><td>Several times steel</td><td>Several times steel</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Start with steel in your new gun (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the details</summary><ul><li><strong>Bismuth:</strong> softer than steel, closer to lead. Kinder to older guns and fixed chokes <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><strong>Tungsten</strong> and TSS (tungsten super shot): very dense, hit hard at range <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Price in CAD (Canadian dollars): <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li>Both cost several times more than steel <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Your new 3 inch gun with IC (Improved Cylinder) or M (Modified) chokes shoots steel well. Start with steel (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Where lead shot is allowed. Lead is OK for BC upland birds: grouse, ptarmigan, quail, partridge, pheasant and turkey, unless a local wetland rule applies. Non toxic only for ducks, geese, coots and snipe, and for any hunting in a National Wildlife Area.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lead or non toxic?</text>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"250\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"205\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"250\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" fill-opacity=\".15\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\"><text x=\"102\" y=\"68\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lead OK</text><text x=\"297\" y=\"68\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Non toxic only</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <text x=\"24\" y=\"100\">Grouse</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"124\">Ptarmigan</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"148\">Quail</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"172\">Partridge</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"196\">Pheasant</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"220\">Turkey</text>\n    <text x=\"24\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\">Watch for a local</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\">wetland rule</text>\n    <text x=\"219\" y=\"100\">Ducks</text><text x=\"219\" y=\"124\">Geese</text><text x=\"219\" y=\"148\">Coots</text><text x=\"219\" y=\"172\">Snipe</text>\n    <text x=\"219\" y=\"212\" font-weight=\"bold\">Any hunt in a</text><text x=\"219\" y=\"232\" font-weight=\"bold\">National</text><text x=\"219\" y=\"252\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wildlife Area</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Grouse #6, quail #7.5, 1 to 1 1/8 oz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Lead is legal for upland birds <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Ducks the same day? Carry <strong>only steel</strong> (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full rules</summary><ul><li>Grouse: #6 shot <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Quail: #7.5 shot <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Load: 1 to 1 1/8 oz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Lead is legal for BC upland birds: grouse, ptarmigan, quail, partridge, pheasants and turkey <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. A local restriction may apply near an important wetland <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Lead is banned for ducks, geese, coots and snipe <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Lead is also banned in National Wildlife Areas: any hunting allowed there must use non toxic shot <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Hunting quail and ducks the same day? Carry only steel so you never load lead at the marsh (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Which of your guns is legal for which bird in BC. CZ 457 .22: grouse yes, quail no, ducks no. Tikka .308: grouse yes, quail no, ducks no. 12 gauge shotgun: grouse yes, quail yes, ducks yes with non toxic shot.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Which gun, which bird?</text>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <rect x=\"130\" y=\"40\" width=\"84\" height=\"34\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"62\">Grouse</text>\n    <rect x=\"218\" y=\"40\" width=\"84\" height=\"34\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"62\">Quail</text>\n    <rect x=\"306\" y=\"40\" width=\"84\" height=\"34\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"348\" y=\"62\">Ducks</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"80\" width=\"380\" height=\"64\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"108\">CZ 457</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"128\">.22 LR</text>\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"150\" width=\"380\" height=\"64\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"178\">Tikka</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"198\">.308</text>\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"220\" width=\"380\" height=\"64\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"248\">12 gauge</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\">shotgun</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"172\" y=\"118\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">✓</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"122\" fill=\"#c0392b\">✗</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"122\" fill=\"#c0392b\">✗</text>\n    <text x=\"172\" y=\"188\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">✓</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"192\" fill=\"#c0392b\">✗</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"192\" fill=\"#c0392b\">✗</text>\n    <text x=\"172\" y=\"262\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">✓</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"262\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">✓</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"262\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">✓</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"172\" y=\"136\">head shots</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"278\">non toxic</text></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>.22 LR (long rifle): grouse, ptarmigan or turkey only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. <strong>Head shots</strong> (Tip).</li><li>No rifle of any kind for ducks or geese <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full rules</summary><ul><li>In BC a .22 or other rimfire is legal among game birds for grouse, ptarmigan or turkey only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>A centrefire rifle, like your .308: grouse or ptarmigan only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>So <strong>no .22 for quail</strong> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Of your guns, only the shotgun is legal for quail <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>No rifle of any kind for ducks or geese <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>With the CZ 457: head shots only. A body shot ruins meat or the bird runs (Tip).</li><li>Know your <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Backstop\">Backstop</button>. A .22 LR bullet carries far past a missed grouse (Tip).</li><li>CCI Mini Mag is a common, reliable choice <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Load</th><th>Box</th><th>CAD price</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Winchester Power Point .308 150 gr</td><td>20</td><td>$40.99 to $54.99</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Remington Core Lokt .308 150 gr</td><td>20</td><td>$54.99</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Federal Fusion .308 150 gr</td><td>20</td><td>$45 to $52</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Federal Partition .308 150 gr</td><td>20</td><td>$59.95</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Hornady Precision Hunter .308 178 gr ELD X</td><td>20</td><td>$59 to $73</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Barnes VOR TX .308 168 gr TTSX</td><td>20</td><td>$80 to $90</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Winchester Xpert steel 3 in</td><td>25</td><td>$30 to $35</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Kent Fasteel 2.0</td><td>25</td><td>$37.99</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Federal Black Cloud</td><td>25</td><td>$47.99</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Kent Bismuth</td><td>25</td><td>about $82 to $100</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Winchester Super X Heavy Game Load (upland)</td><td>25</td><td>$17 to $22</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>CCI Mini Mag .22 LR</td><td>100</td><td>$13.79 to $16.99</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>","<ul><li>CAD (Canadian dollars). Price checked 2026-10-01. Search preview prices, verify at checkout.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: scam warning</summary><ul><li>Avoid ammo sites with scam warning signs: bulkammocanada.com, canfirearm.com, mcadamgundealer.com <span class=\"cert c-tip\" title=\"Certainty\">55%</span>. Buy from a known store (Tip).</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Know one load like your own phone number. That load goes in the rifle every time.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Zeroing with one brand, hunting with another.</li><li>Lead shot in your pocket at the marsh.</li><li>Body shots on grouse with the .22.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Tape on each ammo box: gun, load, use. \"Ducks, steel #2\" or \"Deer, zeroed\".</p></aside>","<ul><li>Shot and gun rules read directly in federal and BC law (95 to 99%). Loads and prices: secondary sources (65 to 70%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-2022-105/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Migratory Birds Regulations, 2022 (SOR/2022-105), full text</a>, read directly, current to 2026-09-21: s. 37(1) (only a shotgun, bow or crossbow for migratory game birds), s. 38 (non toxic shot, pigeon and dove exceptions). Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, read directly and checked against the rendered page image. Printed p. 13 (legal methods table, notes 2, 3 and 4, shot ban notice). Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/190_84_01\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting Regulation, BC Reg 190/84</a>, read directly, current to 22 September 2026: s. 17(1)(f) (rifles only for turkey, grouse and ptarmigan among game birds), s. 17(1)(q) (no centrefire for turkey), s. 17(1)(p) and s. 17(2) (non toxic shot for waterfowl, coot and snipe). Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/C.R.C.,_c._1609/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildlife Area Regulations, C.R.C., c. 1609</a>, read directly, current to 2026-09-21: s. 3(1)(b) (no hunting in a National Wildlife Area unless allowed), s. 3.1 and Schedule I.1 (every hunt allowed there is without toxic shot). Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://bcfirearmsacademy.ca/toxic-lead-shot/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Firearms Academy: toxic lead shot</a>, lead for upland, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>Steel shot sizes and speeds: Ducks Unlimited and Outdoor Life via gear research 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>.308 bullet weights and types: gear research 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li>Ammo prices: search previews of Canadian retailer pages, price checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul></details>"]